          "explanation": "Adults 65+ are preferentially recommended an enhanced vaccine -- high-dose, adjuvanted, or recombinant. In FIM12 (about 32,000 adults 65+), high-dose prevented roughly 24% more confirmed flu than standard dose. The tempting wrong answer is skipping it: an older immune system does respond less, but that is the reason for stronger vaccines, not for skipping. Two standard doses are not recommended, and the nasal spray is only approved up to age 49.",
