          "explanation": "Visceral fat behaves like an active gland, continuously releasing inflammatory messengers such as IL-6 and TNF-alpha, which prompt the liver to make CRP. That is why losing it lowers inflammatory markers. The tempting wrong answer is the sprained ankle -- but that is acute inflammation, which rises and resolves in days. A single workout or meal causes brief blips, not the persistent smolder of inflammaging.",
