          "explanation": "In Prather's 2015 study, healthy adults were deliberately exposed to a cold virus; those sleeping under 6 hours were about 4.2 times more likely to get sick than those sleeping over 7. Regular vitamin C, the most tempting answer, does not prevent colds in the general population in Cochrane reviews and only slightly shortens them. Elderberry evidence is thin, and exercise helps most when it is moderate, not extreme.",
