          "explanation": "Lip or tongue swelling with wheezing after a food suggests anaphylaxis, a fast-moving allergic emergency -- use prescribed epinephrine and call 911. The one-sided rash is the tempting choice: it may be shingles and deserves a prompt doctor call, since antivirals work best within about 3 days, but it is amber, not red. A slowly improving cold is green, and a first-day mild fever is usually green or amber.",
